    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0191" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2648: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Provisional President Burgos to President Harding</hi><anchor n="50" xml:id="d62-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I should be pleased if, for the sake of the success of the liberation plan, the
                    mission of the Honorable Sumner Welles should not terminate before the
                    inauguration of the Constitutional President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Vicini
                    Burgos</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d62-f1" n="50" type="source" xml:id="d62-f1-content">
                <p>A similar telegram, undated, was received by the Department Oct. 30, 1922, from
                    the Dominican Commissioners—Archbishop Nouel, Horacio Vasquez, Federico
                    Velasquez, E. Brache, Francisco J. Peynado (file no. 839.00/2647).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
